#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/06-iot_Remote_relay_controller.rst:19
msgid "6. Remote Relay Controller with Blynk"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/06-iot_Remote_relay_controller.rst:28
msgid "This project aims to create a remote relay controller that can be operated through a virtual switch in the Blynk app. When the switch is turned on, it sets the digital pin connected to the relay to HIGH, and when it's turned off, it sets the digital pin to LOW. This allows for easy control of the relay from a distance, effectively creating a remote switch."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/06-iot_Remote_relay_controller.rst:31
msgid "1. Build the Circuit"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/06-iot_Remote_relay_controller.rst:34
msgid "The following example demonstrates using a relay to control an LED module. **While you can connect the relay to other appliances in actual applications, extreme caution is required when dealing with HIGH AC voltage. Improper or incorrect use can lead to severe injury or even death. Therefore, it is intended for people who are familiar with and knowledgeable about HIGH AC voltage. Always prioritize safety.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/06-iot_Remote_relay_controller.rst:39
msgid "The module draws a high current at start-up, so make sure the 9 V battery or an external power supply is plugged into the DC jack of the R4 Minima."
msgstr ""

