msgid "Open the ``06-Remote_relay_controller.ino`` file under the path of ``ultimate-sensor-kit\\code\\iot_project_espc201\\wifi\\06-Remote_relay_controller``, or copy this code into **Arduino IDE**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/06-iot_Remote_relay_controller.rst:131
msgid "The three Blynk lines were copied in the Get Started chapter. Every project of this kit uses the same device, so they never have to be changed - only the Wi-Fi settings below are project specific."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/06-iot_Remote_relay_controller.rst:141
msgid "Type the name and the password of your own Wi-Fi network."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/06-iot_Remote_relay_controller.rst:148
msgid "Select **Arduino UNO R4 Minima** and the right port, then click **Upload**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/06-iot_Remote_relay_controller.rst:150
msgid "Open the Serial Monitor at **115200**. When the board reaches the cloud the log ends with ``Ready``, and every time you move the switch in the app a line appears here:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/06-iot_Remote_relay_controller.rst:159
msgid "That echo is the quickest way to see that the app and the board are really talking."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/06-iot_Remote_relay_controller.rst:164
msgid "Tap the switch: the relay clicks. Tap it again: it clicks back."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/06-iot_Remote_relay_controller.rst:168
msgid "The relay keeps its position after a power cut. When the board reconnects it asks the server for the last value (``Blynk.syncVirtual(V7)``), so the relay returns to the state you left it in instead of always starting switched off."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/06-iot_Remote_relay_controller.rst:177
msgid "4. Code explanation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/06-iot_Remote_relay_controller.rst:179
msgid "**Blynk account and libraries**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/06-iot_Remote_relay_controller.rst:181
msgid "The first three lines say which Blynk device this board belongs to. They come from the device page and are identical in every project of this kit."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/06-iot_Remote_relay_controller.rst:195
msgid "**The serial port that talks to the module**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/06-iot_Remote_relay_controller.rst:197
msgid "The ESPC2-01 works as a modem: the sketch sends it AT commands. On the R4 it is wired to D0/D1, which is ``Serial1``, a hardware port, so 115200 works without bit errors."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/06-iot_Remote_relay_controller.rst:206
msgid "The function ``espModuleInit()`` waits for the module to finish booting and then sends ``ATE0`` to switch the echo off. Without it, the module's start-up log and the echoed commands get mixed into the replies and Blynk cannot read them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/06-iot_Remote_relay_controller.rst:210
msgid "**The relay pin**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/06-iot_Remote_relay_controller.rst:217
msgid "``RelayPin`` is the pin that drives the relay module - D6 here. ``switchStatus`` simply keeps the last value the app sent, so the code can tell \"on\" from \"off\" in one place."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/06-iot_Remote_relay_controller.rst:222
msgid "Some relay modules switch the other way round and close when the pin is **LOW**. If your relay clicks the opposite way to the switch in the app, swap ``HIGH`` and ``LOW`` in the function below - nothing else changes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/06-iot_Remote_relay_controller.rst:226
msgid "**setup()**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/06-iot_Remote_relay_controller.rst:243
msgid "``digitalWrite(RelayPin, LOW)`` right after ``pinMode`` matters: a pin that has just become an output could otherwise start HIGH for a moment and make the relay click at every power-up."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/06-iot_Remote_relay_controller.rst:247
msgid "**loop()**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/06-iot_Remote_relay_controller.rst:256
msgid "``Blynk.run()`` keeps the connection alive. This project has nothing to measure, so the loop does no other work - but it still has to run as fast as possible."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/06-iot_Remote_relay_controller.rst:259
msgid "**BLYNK_CONNECTED() - restore the last state**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/06-iot_Remote_relay_controller.rst:267
msgid "This runs every time the board reaches the server, including after a power cut. ``Blynk.syncVirtual(V7)`` asks for the stored value of the switch, and the server answers by calling ``BLYNK_WRITE(V7)`` - so the relay ends up in the state you left it in."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/06-iot_Remote_relay_controller.rst:271
msgid "**BLYNK_WRITE(V7) - the switch does the work**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/06-iot_Remote_relay_controller.rst:287
msgid "``BLYNK_WRITE(V7)`` runs by itself whenever datastream **V7** changes - you never call it from ``loop()``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/06-iot_Remote_relay_controller.rst:289
msgid "``param.asInt()`` is the new value: ``1`` when the switch is on, ``0`` when it is off."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/06-iot_Remote_relay_controller.rst:290
msgid "The ``Serial.println`` lines are only there for you; they let you watch the switch from the Serial Monitor."
msgstr ""
